From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:30:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] dt: t6050: describe the camera ISP, disabled

Add the T6050 ISP (ADT /arm-io/isp0) and its three DART instances
(/arm-io/dart-isp0) to t6050.dtsi, every node disabled. Nothing binds:
no driver matches apple,t6050-isp, and there is no "isp" alias, so m1n1
skips its ISP firmware reservation and fwdata fixups exactly as today.

The comment records why the node stays disabled: the T6050 ADT marks
the ISP exclave-assigned (exclave services ISPEngine/ISPEngine_EDK) and
lists ISP_CPU/FE/DPRX/SECURE/BE/CLR as no_ps, so only ISP_SYS and
ISPSENS0 are AP-controllable. MMIO, DART addresses and stream remap
match aurora-silicon's T6040 ISP; the mailbox windows follow that
layout and are inferred.

Only t6050.dtsi changes (no build-kernel.sh or board .dts edit), so it
does not conflict with the pending usb/dcp/audio/platform/integration
patches. Decompiled t6050-j716s.dtb differs from the unpatched one only
by the four new disabled nodes and phandle renumbering; the "okay"
node count is unchanged (8). LLVM=1 W=1: no warnings for j716s/j714s.

Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>

---
 dt/t6050.dtsi | 70 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 70 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dt/t6050.dtsi b/dt/t6050.dtsi
index 22ef313..d252345 100644
--- a/dt/t6050.dtsi
+++ b/dt/t6050.dtsi
@@ -601,6 +601,76 @@
 			power-domains = <&ps_spi4>;
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
+
+		/*
+		 * Camera ISP (ADT /arm-io/isp0, dart-isp0). Described for reference
+		 * only and kept disabled: no driver matches "apple,t6050-isp", and
+		 * no "isp" alias exists, so m1n1 neither reserves the ISP firmware
+		 * nor touches the node.
+		 *
+		 * The T6050 ADT marks the ISP as exclave-assigned: isp0 and isp-exclave-proxy
+		 * carry "exclave-assigned" with the exclave services ISPEngine and
+		 * ISPEngine_EDK; the ISP sub-domains (ISP_CPU, ISP_FE, DPRX,
+		 * ISP_SECURE, ISP_BE, ISP_CLR) are no_ps in the ADT PMGR table,
+		 * so the AP has no power-state register for them; only ISP_SYS
+		 * and ISPSENS0 are AP-visible. The coprocessor firmware is
+		 * preloaded by iBoot (pre-loaded = 1, not running).
+		 *
+		 * MMIO and DART addresses equal the T6040 (M4 Pro/Max) ISP's in
+		 * aurora-silicon/linux, as does the DART stream remap (1, 6, 7,
+		 * 10, 11 -> 0). The mbox, gpio and mbox2 windows below follow
+		 * that T6040 layout (coprocessor +0x2924000) and are inferred,
+		 * not verified on T6050. ADT interrupts: 513 514 515 516 526;
+		 * the first is assumed to carry the mailbox.
+		 *
+		 * dart-isp0 streams: 0 = firmware (mapper-isp0), 12 = MPM;
+		 * 4, 5, 8, 9 are exclave streams (epipe0/1, piodma0/1) and must
+		 * never be configured by Linux. The DART has a DAPF filter and
+		 * "manual-availability".
+		 */
+		isp: isp@580000000 {
+			compatible = "apple,t6050-isp";
+			reg = <0x5 0x80000000 0x0 0x1604000>,
+			      <0x5 0x82924000 0x0 0x40>,
+			      <0x5 0x829241d0 0x0 0x20>,
+			      <0x5 0x82924464 0x0 0x10>;
+			reg-names = "coproc", "mbox", "gpio", "mbox2";
+			interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
+			interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 513 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			iommus = <&isp_dart0 0>, <&isp_dart1 0>, <&isp_dart2 0>;
+			power-domains = <&ps_isp_sys>, <&ps_ispsens0>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
+		isp_dart0: iommu@5828c0000 {
+			compatible = "apple,t6050-dart", "apple,t8110-dart";
+			reg = <0x5 0x828c0000 0x0 0xc000>;
+			#iommu-cells = <1>;
+			interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
+			interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 531 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			power-domains = <&ps_isp_sys>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
+		isp_dart1: iommu@5828e0000 {
+			compatible = "apple,t6050-dart", "apple,t8110-dart";
+			reg = <0x5 0x828e0000 0x0 0xc000>;
+			#iommu-cells = <1>;
+			interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
+			interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 531 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			power-domains = <&ps_isp_sys>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
+		isp_dart2: iommu@582900000 {
+			compatible = "apple,t6050-dart", "apple,t8110-dart";
+			reg = <0x5 0x82900000 0x0 0xc000>;
+			#iommu-cells = <1>;
+			interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
+			interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 531 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			power-domains = <&ps_isp_sys>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
 	};
 };
 
-- 
